" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SnowplowBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fills in the endpoint, the header field that keeps the collector from setting a cookie or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recording the request’s address, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let snowplow = try HTTPDestination.snowplow(","    collector: collector,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com","    vendor: \"com.example\",  \/\/ your schemas' Iglu vendor","    appID: \"shop-ios\",","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a self-describing JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", of the schema"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/payload_data\/jsonschema\/1-0-4"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data"},{"type":"text","text":" is an array of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events, one per record, oldest first. Every member of an event is a string, as the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol has them:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"aid","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The app ID the encoder is made with","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"co"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context’s entities (below), as the text of a self-describing JSON array of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contexts"},{"text":"; left out when there are none","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"dtm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ttm","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in epoch milliseconds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a self-describing event","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The platform: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mob"},{"text":" for a phone, pad, watch or Vision Pro, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tv"},{"text":" for an Apple TV, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pc"},{"text":" for a Mac, and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"app"},{"text":" when the record has no device in its context","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID; left out when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"tv","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":", the tracker"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ue_pr"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event, as the text of a self-describing JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"unstruct_event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holding the event’s own self-describing JSON: its schema, ","type":"text"},{"code":"iglu:<vendor>\/<name>\/jsonschema\/<version>-0-0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its data, its stored properties by name","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"duid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"tnuid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_session","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity, whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lasts across sessions, and no ","type":"text"},{"code":"appleIdfv","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"appleIdfa","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or other device identifier. Snowplow’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"domain_sessionid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the session; a record with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session (one tracked by a tracker without ","type":"text"},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or one a store recovered after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a relaunch, which keeps no context) is sent without one, linked to nothing. The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ttm"},{"type":"text","text":", its true timestamp, is the record’s timestamp, as is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dtm"},{"type":"text","text":", so Snowplow’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"derived_tstamp"},{"type":"text","text":" is when the event was tracked, uncorrected for the device’s clock. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is sent: a retried request sends the same body again, so a sent time would be the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attempt’s, and Snowplow would move the event later by however long the retries took."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s schema is named after its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":": version N is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SchemaVer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":". Each version of an event is a breaking change, a SchemaVer MODEL. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compatible change at the same version is an ADDITION, which the tracking plan’s Iglu export"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan\/writeIgluRegistry(to:vendor:registry:)"},{"type":"text","text":") writes for Iglu Server as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-1"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on, each superseding the ones before, so an event naming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" is validated against the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newest of them. A static repository doesn’t supersede: there an event naming "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validated against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N-0-0"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, so the export refuses an addition for one, and a change to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event needs a new version."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":". The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data then validates against the event’s exported schema, which never requires a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"co","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these entities, for the keys the record’s context has values for:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.snowplow\/mobile_context\/jsonschema\/1-0-3","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", both; "},{"code":"NetworkKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if present"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osType"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ios"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tvos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"watchos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"visionos"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osx"},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"osVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceManufacturer"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Apple Inc."},{"type":"text","text":"), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deviceModel"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"networkType"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"offline"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out for a wired or other connection); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"language"},{"type":"text","text":", the locale’s language code"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"iglu:com.snowplowanalytics.mobile\/application\/jsonschema\/1-0-0","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with both a version and a build","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"build"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Iglu doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"take, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is outside the years 0 to 9999, and one whose JSON is over 150,000 bytes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"text":" returns them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" logs and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. The collector answers 200 to every request it can read, and Snowplow validates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the events afterwards: an event whose data its schema rejects, or whose schema the pipeline’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Iglu resolver can’t find, becomes a failed event, kept apart from the warehouse, though the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination counts it as delivered. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes."}]}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/init(vendor:appID:plan:limit:)"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"]}],"references":{"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding/SnowplowBatchEncoder/requests(for:)":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"type":"text","text":" as the tracker protocol’s requests, each within the encoder’s limit, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records left out of them."}],"url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/requests(for:)",